api-cache-heading = API lookup cache
api-cache-description = Successful EasyScholar responses are cached for 72 hours and Semantic Scholar responses for 24 hours. Successful empty journal results expire within 5 minutes. These two caches persist in this profile across restarts, storing only responses and hashed indexes without request URLs or API keys. Concurrent journal queries and known paper identifiers share responses. Successful Chinese supplemental lookups are cached for 10 minutes in this session and are also removed by explicit clearing. Connection tests go online; expiry, eviction, changed queries or credentials and explicit clearing allow fresh requests.
api-cache-clear =
    .label = Clear API lookup cache
api-cache-cleared = API lookup cache cleared. The next lookup will request fresh data; saved item fields are preserved.
api-cache-clearing = Clearing API lookup cache…
api-cache-clear-failed = Could not clear the disk cache. Check profile directory permissions or the plugin version and retry. Saved item fields are preserved.

metadata-update-journal-info =
    .label = Include journal rankings, impact factors and indexes in metadata updates
metadata-update-journal-info-description = An independent Update stage: runs even when bibliographic metadata is unchanged or its review is disabled. Respects blank/overwrite preferences, selected fields and source priorities, and reuses valid cached responses.

menu-group-review = Verification, Versions and Duplicates
workflow-execution-overview = Imports use independent background switches and default to local checking while retaining all items. Configure manual command visibility, execution steps and optional searches under Context menus and core commands.
workflow-compact-menu = Zotero MetaFlow: show only Check and Fix Metadata and Update Metadata
    .label = Show only Check and Fix Metadata and Update Metadata in the context menu
workflow-compact-description = Enabled by default to show only the two core commands. Configure visibility and execution steps within each command below. Disable this option to customize additional menus and placements. Occasional tools also remain available through On-demand tools and shortcuts.
workflow-remote-authors-check = Also verify authors online when checking and fixing
    .label = Also verify authors online when checking and fixing
workflow-remote-authors-description = Off by default to keep local checks fast. This option affects manual checks only, never import checks. Author verification is also available in Update Metadata.
workflow-tool-center = On-demand Tools
workflow-tool-description = Select references in the main window, then run a tool. Metadata is filled according to identity and source validation; merging still requires selecting duplicate groups. Format conversions, replacements and Extra cleanup follow their settings. Hidden tools do not run automatically.
workflow-tool-choice =
    .aria-label = Select an on-demand tool
workflow-run-tool = Run on Main Window Selection
    .label = Run on Main Window Selection
workflow-tool-no-selection = Select editable references in the main window first.
workflow-tool-running = Running the selected tool…
workflow-tool-finished = The tool has finished. Check the latest batch report for details.
duplicates-heading = Duplicate Settings
duplicates-description = Import duplicate handling shares the local-check queue. Keep All is the default. Only choosing Keep New or Keep Existing enables automatic merging of matching DOIs and compatible versions. Other candidates require review.
duplicates-default-heading = Default Action
duplicates-default-aria =
    .aria-label = Default action for newly imported duplicate items
duplicates-default-action-keep = Keep New: retain the newly imported item and merge duplicates
duplicates-default-action-discard = Keep Existing: retain the existing item and merge duplicates
duplicates-default-action-cancel = Keep All: do not merge items automatically
duplicates-default-action-ask = Always Ask: review candidates found during import
duplicates-master-heading = Retained Item
duplicates-master-aria =
    .aria-label = Retained item strategy for bulk merging
duplicates-master-oldest = Oldest Added: retain the earliest added item
duplicates-master-newest = Newest Added: retain the most recently added item
duplicates-master-modified = Recently Modified: retain the most recently modified item
duplicates-master-detailed = Most Detailed: retain the item with the most populated fields and creators
duplicates-concurrency = Concurrent duplicate groups (1–8, default 3)
duplicates-concurrency-aria =
    .aria-label = Concurrent duplicate groups
duplicates-concurrency-invalid = Enter an integer from 1 to 8. Invalid values are not saved.
duplicates-type-heading = Item Types
duplicates-different-types = Allow merging duplicate items of different types
    .label = Allow merging duplicate items of different types
duplicates-type-description = Off by default. Cross-type merging requires an identical DOI and compatible versions. The type with the fewest incompatible fields is selected, and incompatible values are preserved in Extra. Preprints and published versions are never automatically merged together.
duplicates-view-heading = View
duplicates-show-stats = Append duplicate groups/items to the Duplicate Items label
    .label = Append duplicate groups/items to the Duplicate Items label
duplicates-refresh = Refresh Current Library Duplicate Statistics
    .label = Refresh Current Library Duplicate Statistics
