duplicates-import = Import Non-duplicate Decisions…
    .label = Import Non-duplicate Decisions…
duplicates-invalid-data = Invalid non-duplicate data or capacity exceeded (10,000 pairs). Existing records were not overwritten.
duplicates-import-result = Imported { $imported } pairs; skipped { $skipped } existing, missing or unmatched-library pairs.
duplicates-bulk-confirm = Review { $groups } candidate groups and merge eligible records using the retained item strategy. Empty fields are filled and unrelated Extra lines are preserved. Incompatible DOIs, versions and excluded pairs are skipped. Pause or stop from settings; completed merges remain, with native undo recorded per merge.
duplicates-bulk-status = Processed { $completed }/{ $total } groups; merged { $merged } items; failed { $failed } groups.
duplicates-paused = New groups are paused. In-flight commits finish first. Click again to resume.
duplicates-resumed = Bulk merging resumed.
duplicates-cancelled = Stopping: no more merges will start. Completed operations remain.
duplicates-stats-refreshed = Statistics refreshed. Item changes clear old counts instead of displaying stale numbers.
duplicates-already-running = A bulk merge is already running.
duplicates-select-one-library = Select one library before running this duplicate operation. Multiple selected libraries are not resolved automatically.

core-workflows-heading = Context menus and core commands
core-workflows-description = Configure command visibility, execution steps and optional searches in one place. Hiding an entry affects the menu only; automatic imports use their independent switches in General. Author lookup and duplicate scanning run at most once per workflow.
workflow-update-heading = Update Metadata: execution stages
workflow-update-description = Run enabled bibliographic review, formatting, journal metrics and duplicate review in order. Journal metrics can run with bibliographic review disabled. Cancellation stops later stages; earlier saves remain.
workflow-update-bibliographic = Verify bibliographic metadata online and fill automatically
workflow-update-versions = Automatically detect preprints and convert to published version (look up official DOI and journal info for arXiv preprints)
workflow-update-snapshots = Revive web snapshots (sniff scholarly identifiers from bare webpage snapshots and upgrade to journal articles or preprints)
metaref-workflow-update-snapshots = Revive web snapshots (sniff scholarly identifiers from bare webpage snapshots and upgrade to journal articles or preprints)
workflow-update-tldr = Automatically extract Semantic Scholar TL;DR summary (fetch 1-2 sentence AI core argument)
metaref-workflow-update-tldr = Automatically extract Semantic Scholar TL;DR summary (fetch 1-2 sentence AI core argument)
journal-insights-tldr-heading = Core Takeaway (TL;DR)
rule-tool-update-metadata-tldr-saved = Extracted and saved Semantic Scholar TL;DR ({ $target })
workflow-update-format = Apply enabled local format rules afterward (no duplicate scan or extra enrichment)
workflow-check-duplicates = Review duplicates interactively after checking (replaces the duplicate warning scan)
workflow-update-duplicates = Review duplicates interactively after updating (may be slow in a large library)
workflow-search-heading = Fallback searches for online verification (off by default)
workflow-search-description = These options apply to online verification in both core commands. Existing identifiers take priority. Only enabled fallback searches run when identifiers are missing. PDF content stays local and only existing caches are read. Standalone advanced review tools retain full searches.
workflow-scan-pdf = Read DOI/arXiv candidates from PDF caches when identifiers are missing (automatic evidence checks)
workflow-search-title = Search online by title when identifiers are missing (slower; identity checks remain)
workflow-legacy-heading = Automatic enrichment and legacy advanced-rule options
workflow-legacy-description = This long-DOI rule switch remains for legacy direct callers. Local checking never resolves ShortDOIs online. Core online verification resolves identifiers as needed independently of this compatibility switch.

core-feedback-completed = Combined workflow ended with changes and findings from { $stages } stages; open the full report manually from Settings.
core-feedback-cancelled = Combined workflow stopped. Results from { $stages } stages are retained; earlier saves were not reverted.

review-panel-unavailable = Open the Zotero main window to use the review panel.

review-batch-note = Merge selected duplicate groups in one batch ({ $groups } groups). The configured master is retained with attachments, notes, tags and collections. Publication versions are excluded. Check the groups before applying.
review-batch-select-all = Select / clear all
review-batch-group = { $count } items → retain { $id } · { $title }
review-batch-individual = Review individually

review-auto-ambiguous = Multiple different identifier candidates; preserved the item without requesting confirmation.
review-auto-blocked = Source identifier validation failed; preserved the item.
review-auto-conflict = Conflicting item identity; preserved the item without requesting confirmation.
review-auto-evidence = Title or PDF evidence lacks independent year or author agreement; preserved the item.

runtime-data-open = Open Local Runtime Records

data-settings-heading = Data, Cache and Run Feedback
data-settings-description = Zotero stores references and attachments and manages plugin settings. Reusable API responses and runtime summaries are stored separately in the profile directory. Clearing API caches preserves references, settings, saved rankings and runtime records.
runtime-data-policy = Local run records are kept for { $days } days, up to { $count } runs and { $size } MiB. They store summaries, field names, reason codes and local identifiers for up to 50 items; titles, field contents and raw error text are omitted. Truncated reports are marked.
